language 0.1.0
module storage
  means
    Long-term retention of data, its physical organisation, access to it and
    controlled change of the structure of a store.

entity store : thing
  means
    store: a technical system retaining data beyond the single execution that
    produced it.

entity database : thing
  means
    database: a named collection of interrelated data and its schemas, managed
    by a store.

entity collection : thing
  means
    collection: a named set of stored records of one kind or of compatible
    kinds.

entity table : thing
  means
    table: a relational collection of rows organised by named columns.

entity column : thing
  means
    column: a named typed part of the physical structure of a table.

entity index : thing
  means
    index: an auxiliary storage structure speeding up the search for records
    by definite values.

entity transaction : thing
  means
    transaction: a group of operations on a store, regarded within given
    boundaries of atomicity and isolation.

entity migration : thing
  means
    migration: a controlled transformation of the structure or content of a
    store between two definite states.
